Subject: Optimize-Entity-Tracking

Author: VeltisMC Development Team
Date: 2026-06-19

Reason:
Vanilla entity tracking uses a distance-based broadcast that checks
every entity against every nearby player every tick. For servers with
hundreds of entities and dozens of players, this O(n*m) scan dominates
tick time. Moonrise's entity tracker replaces this with spatial data
structures that filter tracking candidates more efficiently.

Impact:
Dramatically reduced CPU usage for entity tracking on servers with
high entity counts. More stable TPS during mob grinders, farms, and
large-scale events.

Migration Note:
This patch enables Moonrise entity tracker. The spatial tracking
data structures are injected via mixins.

diff --git a/net/minecraft/server/level/ChunkMap.java b/net/minecraft/server/level/ChunkMap.java
index 0000000..0000000 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/server/level/ChunkMap.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/server/level/ChunkMap.java
@@ -0,0 +1,10 @@
+// VeltisMC: Moonrise entity tracking optimization
+//
+// Moonrise replaces vanilla ChunkMap entity tracking with a
+// spatial-index-based approach, reducing the cost of finding
+// which entities need to be sent to which players.
+//
+// Implemented by mixins:
+//   - entity_tracker.ChunkMapMixin
+//   - entity_tracker.EntityMixin
+//   - entity_tracker.TrackedEntityMixin
